WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:05.043
Nadia is the M&E officer at Meridian.

2
00:00:05.043 --> 00:00:10.720
Every figure a field team sends lands here, in Review, before it counts anywhere.

3
00:00:11.132 --> 00:00:15.512
Today she works through Kurigram, the literacy project in Bangladesh,

4
00:00:15.512 --> 00:00:18.115
so she filters the queue to that project.

5
00:00:18.561 --> 00:00:22.241
First, the teacher training figure for October to December,

6
00:00:22.241 --> 00:00:23.800
which Farhana sent today.

7
00:00:24.206 --> 00:00:27.071
Twelve teachers, with no evidence attached.

8
00:00:27.508 --> 00:00:31.032
Before deciding, she asks a question in the comments.

9
00:00:31.032 --> 00:00:34.689
Farhana gets a notification and can reply on her phone.

10
00:00:35.096 --> 00:00:39.570
Without the sign-in sheets she can't confirm the number, so she returns it,

11
00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.479
and says exactly what is needed.

12
00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.877
The figure goes back to Farhana with the reason.

13
00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:48.672
It stays out of dashboards and reports until she corrects it.

14
00:00:49.091 --> 00:00:51.968
Next, a figure that came back to her corrected:

15
00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:54.417
girls' attendance for the third quarter.

16
00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:55.961
This is round two.

17
00:00:55.961 --> 00:00:59.971
Earlier today she returned it and asked for the class registers.

18
00:00:59.971 --> 00:01:03.479
The audit trail keeps that first round, with her reason.

19
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.942
Now the registers are attached, and Farhana replied in the thread:

20
00:01:07.942 --> 00:01:11.616
the rate is final, ninety-one percent, from all six schools.

21
00:01:12.053 --> 00:01:13.634
The registers match.

22
00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.199
She approves it, and notes what she checked.

23
00:01:17.199 --> 00:01:20.692
Before, a figure she had returned could get stuck waiting.

24
00:01:20.692 --> 00:01:22.860
Now the new round is hers to decide.

25
00:01:23.271 --> 00:01:26.637
Approved, and published into dashboards and reports.

26
00:01:27.048 --> 00:01:31.460
On the indicator page, the third quarter now shows ninety-one percent,

27
00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.541
against a target of eighty-seven.

28
00:01:33.953 --> 00:01:35.428
That is the review step.

29
00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:39.361
Questions in the thread, clear reasons when something goes back,

30
00:01:39.361 --> 00:01:41.450
and a full history of every round.
